    "source": "Final NVIDIA dual-view run, actual owned editor client area; visually inspected on both tested GPUs."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Correctness fixtures on one Windows laptop with NVIDIA RTX 4070 Laptop and AMD Radeon integrated graphics; not game-scale performance or broad hardware qualification.",
    "GUI input is scoped synthetic HWND messages and relative-motion events; physical mouse capture, input feel, IME, accessibility and multi-display/DPI behavior require further qualification.",
    "Both viewports own separate Vulkan devices/resources and render serially on the creating UI thread. One shared owner poll drives simulation; no concurrent-rendering or latency claim.",
    "Full device-loss recovery and Khronos Vulkan validation are not qualified; recorded zero-error counts are NVRHI diagnostics.",
    "The full profiler, Scene orientation widget, camera frustums and component visualization are planned; this milestone adds independent panels and layout behavior."
  ],
  "observations": [
    "An earlier sky GUI run changed selection before its final capture; the cause was not established. Its local evidence was retained as failed on review. The strengthened harness asserts native and Inspector selection at both final capture stages; both final GPU reruns passed without a production binary change."
  ]
